<!--
  ============================================================================
  AnimalBiomeDuplicates_Fix.xml            Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-10
  ============================================================================

  THE BUG
  =======
  RimWorld builds each biome's animal table in BiomeDef.CommonalityOfAnimal()
  by adding entries to a Dictionary keyed on PawnKindDef. An animal can reach a
  biome from TWO directions:

      (a) the BiomeDef lists it      :  <wildAnimals><Foo>0.2</Foo></wildAnimals>
      (b) the animal lists the biome :  <race><wildBiomes><Bar>0.3</Bar></...>

  If the SAME animal arrives from BOTH directions for the SAME biome, the
  dictionary Add() throws:

      System.ArgumentException: An item with the same key has already been added.

  That exception is NOT contained. Every consumer that enumerates AllWildAnimals
  dies with it. Observed live on this stack, 2026-08-10:

      * Choose Wild Animal Spawns   : static ctor throws, MOD IS DEAD at startup
      * Giddy-Up                    : "error calling AllWildAnimals ... Skipping",
                                      BuildAnimalBiomeCache() never completes
      * Biome Compatibility Project : PatchCreaturesToBiomes() throws inside
                                      LongEventHandler.ExecuteToExecuteWhenFinished,
                                      ABORTING THE REST OF THE POST-LOAD QUEUE

  Two bad entries were silently degrading three unrelated systems.

  DETECTION
  =========
  Found by Utils/animal_inventory.py, which reads every active mod's Defs and
  cross-references (a) against (b) in BOTH directions. Output: conflicts.csv.
  Exactly 3 duplicate (biome, animal) pairs existed across 1,168 animals.
  Re-run that script after any mod update to re-check.

  DESIGN
  ======
  Always remove the (b) side, the animal's <wildBiomes> entry, and never the
  biome's <wildAnimals> list. Rationale:
    * the biome side is usually vanilla/DLC and should not be touched;
    * removing the animal-side entry leaves the animal still spawning in that
      biome via the biome's own list, at the biome's commonality.
  Net effect on gameplay: NOTHING is lost. Only the duplicate registration goes.

  SAFETY
  ======
  Every op is wrapped in PatchOperationConditional testing that the exact node
  exists. If a mod is not loaded, or the author fixes their def in an update,
  the op becomes a silent no-op instead of a red error. Load this mod LAST.

  TARGETS AND SOURCES
  ===================
  Armadillo  [VERIFIED 2026-08-10; source and load order RE-VERIFIED 2026-08-14]
      CORE     Data/Core/Defs/BiomeDefs/Biomes_WarmArid.xml lists
               <Armadillo MayRequire="Ludeon.RimWorld.Odyssey">0.2 in BOTH
               AridShrubland (L147) and Desert (L305)  (biome side, keep).
               NOTE: the biome file is CORE's, not Odyssey's - only the entry
               is Odyssey-gated. Do not go looking for it under Data/Odyssey.
      Odyssey  Races_Animal.xml Armadillo ThingDef declares NO wildBiomes,
               so the xpaths below cannot touch vanilla
      Beasts of the Rim (Continued), WS 2194018641, mlie.beastsoftherim, is the
               SOLE animal-side contributor - re-verified by grepping the whole
               workshop tree, plus every wildBiomes-touching PatchOperation, for
               an indirect xpath route. There is none.
               It redefines the Armadillo defName in
               1.6/Defs/ThingDefs_Races/Races_Animal_Armadillo.xml (L93-97) and
               adds wildBiomes: AridShrubland 0.3, Desert 0.3, ExtremeDesert 0.3.
               The first two collide. ExtremeDesert does NOT (vanilla omits
               Armadillo there), so it is LEFT IN PLACE.
      ORDER    mlie.beastsoftherim is at 63, mandrake.jawa.patches at 581, so
               we load 518 slots later and the conditional SEES the duplicate.
               This op is firing, not silently no-opping.

  🔴 STALE AFTER THE 2026-09-05 RETIREMENTS - REGENERATE ON THE NEXT CAPTURE.
      Megafauna, Beasts of the Rim, Mythic Ages and Jurassic Rimworld were retired
      that day (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/RETIREMENT_CHECKLIST.md). Seven operations
      whose defNames belonged only to those mods were deleted, so the numbering in
      the comments below now has gaps. What could NOT be deleted by name is the
      Armadillo and Penguin work: those defNames are vanilla AND redefined by Beasts
      of the Rim, and it was Beasts of the Rim that added the colliding animal-side
      entry. With that mod gone the vanilla defs carry no wildBiomes at all, so each
      of those conditionals simply matches nothing - dead, not harmful. Re-run
      src/RimMandrake/Utils/biome_animal_conflicts.py against a capture taken after
      the mods are actually unticked; it needs a LIVE dump, which is why this was
      left rather than guessed at.

  Titan      [VERIFIED 2026-08-10]
      Titans, WS 3572242808, Defs/ThingDefs_Races/Races_Animal_Titan.xml lists
      <TropicalSwamp>1.0</TropicalSwamp> TWICE inside its own <wildBiomes>.
      Self-inflicted, nothing else involved. We drop the second occurrence.
      Report upstream; this patch is the local stopgap.
  ============================================================================
-->
<Patch>

  <!-- ==================================================================
       1. Armadillo x AridShrubland
       Beasts of the Rim's animal-side entry duplicates Odyssey's biome-side
       entry. Remove the animal-side one; Odyssey's 0.2 commonality still
       spawns armadillos in arid shrubland.
       ================================================================== -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Armadillo"]/race/wildBiomes/AridShrubland</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationRemove">
      <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Armadillo"]/race/wildBiomes/AridShrubland</xpath>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- ==================================================================
       2. Armadillo x Desert
       Same shape as above. Odyssey's biome-side 0.2 remains authoritative.
       ================================================================== -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Armadillo"]/race/wildBiomes/Desert</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationRemove">
      <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Armadillo"]/race/wildBiomes/Desert</xpath>
    </match>
  </Operation>

  <!-- ==================================================================
       3. Titan x TropicalSwamp  (duplicate WITHIN one mod's own def)
       The Titans mod lists TropicalSwamp twice in the same <wildBiomes>.
       The [2] predicate selects the SECOND occurrence only. A bare
       .../TropicalSwamp xpath would match BOTH, and PatchOperationRemove
       deletes every match, which would strip titans from the biome
       entirely. Keep the first, drop the second.
       The conditional also tests [2], so if Titans fixes their file this
       becomes a no-op automatically.
       ================================================================== -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationConditional">
    <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Titan"]/race/wildBiomes/TropicalSwamp[2]</xpath>
    <match Class="PatchOperationRemove">
      <xpath>/Defs/ThingDef[defName="Titan"]/race/wildBiomes/TropicalSwamp[2]</xpath>
    </match>
  </Operation>

